  "tagline": "Qihoo 360's Redis-compatible, RocksDB-backed store for datasets too big for memory.",
  "description": "Pika (now branded PikiwiDB in its OpenAtom Foundation repository) was built at Qihoo 360 to keep Redis's protocol and operating model while storing data in RocksDB on disk. It targets the point where Redis instances grow beyond tens of gigabytes and start suffering from slow restarts, large replication buffers and memory cost. It supports the common Redis data types, slaveof-style replication and Codis-based clustering, and is heavily used in China. Outside that ecosystem documentation is thinner, much of it in Chinese.",
